Join the millions of people who love the Life Bible App (formerly Tecarta Bible). Our mission is to help people get the most out of their Bibles everyday. Start every morning with the verse of the day, daily devotional or daily TouchPoint - Bible answers for life’s most important questions. 

Whether you are a beginner or veteran, you can find everything you need to deepen your relationship with God and grow. There are thousands of free Bible reading plans and devotionals if you need some help on what to read in the morning. Already know what you want to study? Select from the collection of Study Bibles and Commentaries to help you go deeper. Or create your own plans.

Need help understanding a verse or just simply want to know more? With just one tap, find the meaning behind every Bible verse (Explain) or see the verse in other Bible translations (Compare). Easily share with your friends.

STUDY GOD’S WORD

∙ In this Bible app, stream popular translations for free such as the NLT, NIV, KJV, ESV, CSB, NASB, NKJV, AMP, MESSAGE and many more including Spanish and Chinese translations. Download any title for offline access;
∙ Search has never been easier or faster. Other Bible apps search only a single translation. The Life Bible App searches over 40 translations simultaneously to find your Bible verse. Use the filter to select your favorite Bible translations;
∙ The only Bible app to have the best-selling TouchPoints series available for free. Discover over 350 topics with engaging questions and Scriptures to find Bible answers for life’s most important questions;
∙ Listen to an audio Bible to study God’s Word on the go;
∙ Explore and try for free all the best-selling Study Bibles to help you understand the meaning and background of Scripture. Here are some of our favorites:
- Life Application Study Bible
- NIV Study Bible
- KJV Study Bible
- ESV Study Bible
- CSB Study Bible
- MacArthur Study Bible
∙ Commentaries include Cornerstone Bible Commentary, Life Application Bible Commentary, Thru the Bible Commentary, Jon Courson’s Application Commentary, Believer’s Bible Commentary, Matthew Henry Concise Commentary and the Preacher’s Commentary.

DAILY BIBLE PLANS AND DEVOTIONALS

∙ Get daily Bible app notifications each morning for the Bible verse of the day and daily devotional;
∙ Looking to study a devotional topic? Choose from over 600 topics for your daily reading;
∙ Start a Bible reading plan by choosing a One-year Bible, The Bible Recap, Chronological Bible, Psalms, Proverbs, Old Testament, New Testament or create your own plan;
∙ The Life Bible App allows you to create free 3, 7, 14 or 30 day devotional plans.

THE MOST POWERFUL BIBLE APP

∙ Designed by developers and designers who love the Bible;
∙ Choose your own unique highlight colors to markup important verses and insights in your Bible app;
∙ Create personal study notes in the Bible app with our “verse notes” feature! See your personal insights as you read through the Bible;
∙ Easily take notes with our “quick-paste” feature. Flip seamlessly between your Bible and notes so you don’t get left behind during church. Rich text editor allows you to bold, underline, indent or create numbered and bulleted lists;
∙ Split the screen so you can see Bibles, Study Bibles, commentaries or personal notes side by side;
∙ Backup & sync your Bible app. Access notes, bookmarks, highlights and purchases across all your mobile and web devices for easy access anywhere;
∙ Customize your Bible study settings to change font, font size, and light/dark mode;
∙ Share verses with family and friends via email, text, Twitter or Facebook.

Check out the Life Bible website at lifebible.com.

Have any suggestions (content or features) you would like to see offered in our Bible app? Email us at biblesupport@tecarta.com

Jean-Frédéric Osterwald (ou Ostervald) (25 Novembre 1663 à 1614 Avril, 1747), pasteur protestant suisse, est né à Neuchâtel en 1663 dans une famille patricienne, un fils du pasteur réformé Johann Rudolf Ostervald. Il a étudié à Zurich et à Saumur (où il a obtenu), étudia la théologie à Orléans, sous Claude Pajon, à Paris sous Jean Claude et à Genève sous Louis Tronchin, et a été ordonné au ministère dans sa ville natale en 1683.

Français Bible Ostervald, une révision de la traduction française, en particulier, a longtemps été connue et très appréciée en Grande-Bretagne.

Avantages de l'application:
- L'application fonctionne sans connexion Internet (hors ligne);
- Possibilité de rechercher;
- Possibilité pour augmenter / diminuer la police;
- Possibilité de créer un nombre illimité d'onglets à un verset particulier, l'un des livres;
- Si vous êtes intéressé à la répartition des poèmes que vous pouvez copier ou envoyer un message;
- Possibilité de faire défiler les boutons de volume.
Notre équipe est pas en place, et vise à élargir ses applications fonctionnelles.

Mode d'emploi:
Chaque élément de menu est un livre séparé, et chaque page séparée dans l'un des livres est la tête.
Placez le curseur à la place du numéro de chapitre et entrez le numéro de chapitre. Ainsi, vous ne serez pas avoir à faire défiler tous les chapitres, la sélection intéressante.

